From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:45:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 103/111] regulator: rt5739: support the RT5738

From lidar-mainline by LeagueRaINi (GPL-2.0, commit db8242a), backported
to 6.12 for the MT8516 Echos (ADR 0031).

The MT8516 Echos take the CPU supply (Vproc) from a Richtek RT5738 on
I2C at 0x57: lidar-mainline's device tree, and Amazon's donut.dtsi and
cupcake.dtsi. It uses the RT5739 register map and its 300-1300 mV range
in 5 mV steps; on an Echo Plus (2nd gen) PVT unit its ID registers read
0, so it is matched by its compatible and never given the RT5733 table.
---
 .../bindings/regulator/richtek,rt5739.yaml         |  3 +++
 drivers/regulator/rt5739.c                         | 14 +++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/richtek,rt5739.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/richtek,rt5739.yaml
index e95e046e9..282cd8342 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/richtek,rt5739.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/richtek,rt5739.yaml
@@ -15,6 +15,8 @@ description: |
   supply of 2.5V to 5.5V. It can provide up to 3.5A continuous current
   capability at over 80% high efficiency.
 
+  The RT5738 uses the RT5739 register map and voltage range.
+
 allOf:
   - $ref: regulator.yaml#
 
@@ -22,6 +24,7 @@ properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
       - richtek,rt5733
+      - richtek,rt5738
       - richtek,rt5739
 
   reg:
diff --git a/drivers/regulator/rt5739.c b/drivers/regulator/rt5739.c
index 91412c905..6633e7831 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/rt5739.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/rt5739.c
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
 #define RT5733_VOLT_STPUV	6250
 #define RT5733_N_VOLTS		182
 
+#define RT5739_CHIPDIE_ID	0x0
 #define RT5739_VOLT_MINUV	300000
 #define RT5739_VOLT_MAXUV	1300000
 #define RT5739_VOLT_STPUV	5000
@@ -253,6 +254,7 @@ static int rt5739_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 	struct regulator_dev *rdev;
 	bool vsel_acth;
 	unsigned int vid;
+	u8 did;
 	int ret;
 
 	desc = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*desc), GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -279,7 +281,16 @@ static int rt5739_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 
 	vsel_acth = device_property_read_bool(dev, "richtek,vsel-active-high");
 
-	rt5739_init_regulator_desc(desc, vsel_acth, vid & RT5739_DID_MASK);
+	did = vid & RT5739_DID_MASK;
+	/*
+	 * RT5738 shares the RT5739 register map and its 300-1300 mV range in
+	 * 5 mV steps. Its die ID is not documented, so never let it select
+	 * the RT5733 voltage table.
+	 */
+	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "richtek,rt5738"))
+		did = RT5739_CHIPDIE_ID;
+
+	rt5739_init_regulator_desc(desc, vsel_acth, did);
 
 	cfg.dev = dev;
 	cfg.of_node = dev_of_node(dev);
@@ -293,6 +304,7 @@ static int rt5739_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 
 static const struct of_device_id rt5739_device_table[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "richtek,rt5733" },
+	{ .compatible = "richtek,rt5738" },
 	{ .compatible = "richtek,rt5739" },
 	{ /* sentinel */ }
 };
